  "status_text": "One more pair means six times as many possible conversations. Lean checked a three-choice setup where every pair of opening replies shares a valid choice, and each choice misses some reply on each side. One reader sends a message and the other answers. Together those public messages determine valid choices for all the independent pairs. Each extra pair triples the minimum number of possible opening messages and multiplies the minimum number of distinct message pairs by six. One protocol reaches both minima (L-meta-38162).",
